+### Step 0b: Detect Reviewer Mode
+
+Determine which reviewer backend to use. If `REVIEWER_MODE` is explicitly set to `codex` or `subagent`, use that. Otherwise (`auto`), detect at runtime:
+
+```
+1. Try calling mcp__codex__codex with a no-op ping (e.g., prompt: "Reply OK")
+2. If the tool exists and responds → REVIEWER_BACKEND = "codex"
+3. If the tool errors, times out, or is not found → REVIEWER_BACKEND = "subagent"
+```
+
+Log the chosen backend in `PAPER_IMPROVEMENT_LOG.md`:
+```
+Reviewer backend: codex (GPT-5.4 via Codex MCP)
+— or —
+Reviewer backend: subagent (Claude domain-reviewer agent)
+```
+
+> ⚠️ The subagent reviewer uses a fresh Claude agent with the `architect-reviewer` type and a detailed paper-review system prompt. It produces the same structured output format (score, strengths, weaknesses, fixes, verdict) so all downstream steps work identically regardless of backend.
+
